<Project>
  <!--
    ADR 0098 §1: the single version of everything Kazo OS publishes (SDK, platform, base apps,
    Kazo.Os.App.Build, Kazo.Os.Ecosystem.Host, templates). Imported by Directory.Build.props, so
    every project of the solution carries it; Platform/Packaging.props inherits it.

    Before the SDK 1.0 freeze: 0.9.0-preview.<n>. Since the freeze (chantier v3/15, ADR 0114):
    SemVer (ADR 0019) - patch with no API change, minor for an addition, major for a breaking
    change of the SDK. PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt of each library says which one a release needs.
    1.1.0 (chantier v3.1/4-sdk-1-1, ADR 0117 §5): window title, window geometry opt-out, user
    accounts and passwd, per-user default handlers.
    1.2.0 (chantier exec/10-final, ADR 0132 §2): process limits, niceness, OOM score adjustment,
    KazoBackground and its analyzer, KazoWireContext for remote gateways, all published once at the
    end of the exec series.
    2.0.0 (chantier desk/6-sdk-2, ADR 0149, ADR 0161): Kazo.Os.AppSdk.FileView leaves the SDK for
    the contracts the OS provides at run time (KazoFileView, the OS context menu, file menu entries,
    desktop settings) and KazoFileOperations; an app built on 1.x is refused and must be rebuilt.
    2.1.0 (ADR 0173, first automatic release): additions since 2.0 (passkeys, user administration,
    KazoFileView.OpenOnTap, ParentExitGracePeriod...) folded into PublicAPI.Shipped.txt. Since ADR
    0173, changing this number and merging into main is the whole release: the Release Kazo OS
    workflow tags the commit, creates the GitHub Release and pushes the packages to nuget.org.
    2.2.0 (series todo/base, Kazo OS Store ADR 0206 to 0208, 0212, 0213): kazoos-solution template
    and its external-source build (Kazo.Os.ExternalSource.targets), installed-app wwwroot served by
    the service worker, trusted sources, per-user installs and build-time source/block-list defaults,
    the Kazo OS Store app and catalog installs, theme packs, plus wallpaper images, icon packs, cursor
    themes, system sounds, notification toasts, window animations and taskbar previews, all folded
    into PublicAPI.Shipped.txt (ADR 0207 §11: the template's Release profile needs this version).
    2.2.1 (Benoit's choice of a patch number, 2026-11-01, although the public API grows): every
    static resource of an app in its package and an installed app's scoped CSS (ADR 0221), the
    satellite assemblies of installed apps (ADR 0222), the authors' signing tool (ADR 0219), mouse
    Back/Forward buttons (ADR 0220), restart onto the new version (ADR 0223), do not disturb,
    wallpaper menus and the mobile home wallpaper (ADR 0216 to 0218), all folded into
    PublicAPI.Shipped.txt. Apps waiting for the Kazo OS Store build their packages with it.
    2.2.2 (2026-11-01): the official catalog's public key compiled into the OS
    (AppPackageDefaults.OfficialCatalogSigningKey): every Kazo OS Store package must carry the
    catalog's signature. No SDK change: only that Platform.Core constant moves in the API files.
    3.0.0 (series rename/base, ADR 0228, ADR 0229): HackerOS becomes Kazo OS. Every package moves
    from HackerOs.* to Kazo.Os.* and every SDK type from Hack* to Kazo* (HackFile -> KazoFile...);
    an app built on 2.x is refused and must be rebuilt against Kazo.Os.AppSdk.
    3.1.0 (series os-3-1/base, ADR 0234): WinForms-like window styles (Normal, Tool, transparent
    None) and their options, app window control (minimize, maximize, move, resize), child windows
    and modal dialogs (ShowWindowAsync, ShowDialogAsync), file dialogs that start in an existing
    folder, capabilities of an app installed during the session, network drives readable by apps
    (ADR 0231), illustrated app icons (ADR 0232) and the real network for chat apps (WebSocket,
    relay TLS, declared ports, ADR 0235), all folded into PublicAPI.Shipped.txt.
    3.2.0 (ADR 0233): the server issues the real-network grant approved in the OS, with the ports
    the app declares, so a third-party app (the IRC app) reaches its ports through the relay;
    Platform Core and Server Contracts API folded into PublicAPI.Shipped.txt.
    3.2.1 (2026-11-08, patch): the rename migration of 3.0.0 writes the new hash of the rewritten
    configuration files, and a one-time boot repair gives back the files 3.0.0 to 3.2.0 left on
    deleted content (ProviderFailure on /etc/kazoos/app-permissions.config). No SDK change: only
    the Infrastructure.Browser repair entry points move in the API files.
    3.3.0 (2026-11-11): build number and version status at sign-in (ADR 0236), the OS and its apps
    start on the latest version (ADR 0237, 0239, 0241), an app failure stays in its window
    (ADR 0238), a detailed error page with secrets masked (ADR 0240), allowing a capability for the
    machine withdraws the user's own refusal, and installed apps find System.Private.CoreLib whole
    with an exact install check (ADR 0242). SDK additions (App Abstractions, AppSdk.Blazor) and the
    host, platform and browser API folded into PublicAPI.Shipped.txt.
    3.3.4 (2026-11-13, Benoit's choice of a patch number although the public API grows, like 3.3.3):
    a Craft app's exports reach its window (ADR 0264, for Kazo Pdf), the direct link survives the
    restart for an update (ADR 0265) and the new Kazo OS Store home, app page, install progress and
    phone layout (ADR 0266, InstallAsync overload with IProgress), all folded into
    PublicAPI.Shipped.txt.
    3.3.3 (2026-11-13, Benoit's choice of a patch number although the public API grows, like 2.2.1):
    direct app launch link ?autolaunch=<appId> (ADR 0258), the shared Craft apps module
    Kazo.Os.AppSdk.Craft (ADR 0259), windows that stay on their screen (window.canChangeScreen,
    ADR 0263) and Store apps offered for a file no app opens (ADR 0257), all folded into
    PublicAPI.Shipped.txt. Kazo Word 0.1.1 and Kazo Spreadsheets build against it.
    3.3.2 (2026-11-13, patch): a file may be 128 MiB instead of 16 MiB, written and read in 16 MiB
    batches (ADR 0245), so Kazo Word installs. No SDK API change: only the value of
    Infrastructure.Browser's FileContentStoragePolicy.DefaultMaxFileSizeBytes moves in the API files.
    3.4.0 is kept for the prerelease SDK of Os#456.
    3.3.1 (2026-11-13, patch): the published service worker serves an installed app's page loaded
    in a frame (ADR 0243), and windows keep their place in the page so a window coming to the front
    no longer reloads its frames (ADR 0244). No SDK change: only Windowing.Core's
    WindowDocumentOrder moves in the API files.

    The App SDK version an app is compiled against comes from this number (KazoOsSdk.Version), and
    the manifest generator writes it as the app's sdkCompatibility.minimumVersion (ADR 0098 §3).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <KazoOsVersion>3.3.4</KazoOsVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
